FakeStreamHandle::stopSending fired the write cancel token before it finished
updating the handle. The fake wires both sessions together on one thread, so
the peer reacts inside that call. A peer that closes the session then destroys
the handle, and the rest of stopSending touched freed memory. Fire the token
last, as resetStream already does.

Add deliverPeerReset, which fails a read half without resetting the writer.
resetStream also fires the writer's cancel token, so a session on the writing
side reacts to its own reset and the reader cannot see a RESET_STREAM alone.

